---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import AgentDiagram from '../../components/diagrams/AgentDiagram.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Agentic AI system"
  summary="A tool-using agent that answers operational questions end to end — with an eval harness that says how often it is actually right."
  metaDescription="Agentic AI system by Quoc Nguyen: a tool-using agent with retrieval, SQL and actions, evaluated against a golden scenario suite."
  stack={['Python', 'RAG→Agents', 'eval harnesses', 'Docker', 'CI']}
  nextSteps={[
    'TODO: honest next step — e.g. widen the golden set to cover multi-turn sessions.',
    'TODO: honest next step — e.g. add online eval sampling from production traces.',
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="links">
    <span class="font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.04em] text-muted">live demo — TODO: url</span>
    <span class="font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.04em] text-muted">repo — TODO: url</span>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="problem">
    <p>
      TODO: replace with the real problem story. The shape of it: people burn time digging
      answers out of scattered docs and databases by hand, and a plain chatbot gives fluent
      answers with no guarantee they are grounded in anything.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted">
      Without a measured agent, every answer is a judgment call: nobody can say whether the
      system is right 9 times out of 10 or 6, so nobody can safely rely on it. The eval
      harness exists to turn "it seems fine" into a number that can be defended.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="diagram"><AgentDiagram /></Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="diagram-caption">
    Fig. 02 — Request flow: the agent loop calls retrieval, SQL and action tools; every
    trace is scored by the eval harness.
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="evaluation">
    <div class="max-w-[60ch]">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">Measured</span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
        Three things: end-to-end task success on a golden scenario suite, tool-call success
        (did the agent call the right tool with valid arguments), and p50 latency per answer.
      </p>
      <span class="mt-8 block font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted"
        >Eval design</span
      >
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        TODO: real eval details. Template: a golden set of N scenarios with known-correct
        answers, scored by exact-match checks where possible and an LLM judge with a written
        rubric where not, with a human spot-check on a sample of judge decisions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid max-w-[720px] grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">87%</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Eval pass rate
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">1.4s</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          p50 latency
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">94%</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Tool-call success
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[720px] overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left">
        <caption class="caption mb-4 text-left text-muted">Results by configuration</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">Metric</th>
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">RAG baseline</th>
            <th class="py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">Agent</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="font-mono text-[13px] text-ink">
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Task success</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">TODO</td>
            <td class="py-3">87%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Tool-call success</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">n/a</td>
            <td class="py-3">94%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">p50 latency</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">TODO</td>
            <td class="py-3">1.4s</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[60ch]">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted"
        >What failed → what was fixed</span
      >
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        TODO: the real failure story. Template: early runs lost most failures to malformed
        tool arguments, not wrong reasoning — adding JSON-schema validation with a single
        structured retry moved tool-call success from its baseline to the number above.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</ProjectLayout>
